<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Vega-Lite → Altair / vega-lite-api / D3 / ggplot2 — showcase</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/style.css">
</head>
<body>
<header class="site-header">
  <a href="https://vega.github.io/vega-lite/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Vega-Lite</a>
  <h1>Translation Showcase</h1>
  <span class="sub">{{ total_count }} example specs · 4 target systems each</span>
  <a class="github-link" href="https://github.com/datamazelab/vl2x" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
</header>
<main>
  <h1>Example Gallery</h1>
  <p class="intro">
    Organized like the official
    <a href="https://vega.github.io/vega-lite/examples/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Vega-Lite example gallery</a>
    ({{ gallery_count }} of these examples come straight from it, grouped the
    same way; the rest are additional test-corpus specs grouped below that).
    Every spec is translated by four sibling code generators —
    <strong>vl2altair</strong> (Python/Altair), <strong>vl2vlapi</strong>
    (JavaScript/vega-lite-api), <strong>vl2d3</strong> (JavaScript/D3), and
    <strong>vl2ggplot</strong> (R/ggplot2). Click a thumbnail to see the
    generated code and rendered chart side by side for each.
<HR>
    Note that these are direct transpiles from the source vega-lite JSON. In some cases (largely D3 and ggplot2), this will not render correctly or at all. This does not mean that it is not possible to construct equivalent visualizations. It just can't be done simply through transforming the JSON to code.
  </p>

  <div class="controls">
    <input type="search" id="search" placeholder="Search by name or description…">
    <select id="support-filter">
      <option value="all">All support levels</option>
      <option value="all-ok">All 4 systems succeed</option>
      <option value="any-fail">At least 1 system fails/unsupported</option>
      <option value="none-ok">All 4 systems fail/unsupported</option>
    </select>
  </div>
  <div class="stat-summary" id="stat-summary"></div>

  <nav class="toc">
    {% for section in sections %}
    <a href="#{{ section.slug }}">{{ section.h2 }}</a>
    {% endfor %}
  </nav>

  <div id="grid-root">
    {% for section in sections %}
    <section class="section-block" data-section>
      <h2 class="section-h2" id="{{ section.slug }}">{{ section.h2 }}</h2>
      {% for sub in section.subsections %}
      <div class="sub-block" data-subsection>
        {% if sub.h3 %}<h3 class="section-h3">{{ sub.h3 }}</h3>{% endif %}
        <div class="gallery">
          {% for ex in sub.cards %}
          <a class="imagegroup" href="examples/{{ ex.name }}/index.html"
             data-name="{{ ex.name }}" data-desc="{{ ex.description }}"
             data-status="{{ ex.altair_ok and 'ok' or 'fail' }},{{ ex.vlapi_ok and 'ok' or 'fail' }},{{ ex.d3_ok and 'ok' or 'fail' }},{{ ex.ggplot_ok and 'ok' or 'fail' }}">
            {% if ex.has_thumb %}
            <span class="thumb" style="background-image: url('thumbs_png/{{ ex.name }}.png')"></span>
            {% else %}
            <span class="thumb no-thumb">no preview</span>
            {% endif %}
            <span class="image-title">{{ ex.title }}</span>
            <span class="image-badges">
              <span class="badge {{ ex.altair_ok and 'ok' or 'fail' }}">Altair</span>
              <span class="badge {{ ex.vlapi_ok and 'ok' or 'fail' }}">vlapi</span>
              <span class="badge {{ ex.d3_ok and 'ok' or 'fail' }}">D3</span>
              <span class="badge {{ ex.ggplot_ok and 'ok' or 'fail' }}">ggplot2</span>
            </span>
          </a>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </section>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</main>
<footer class="site-footer">vl2altair · vl2vlapi · vl2d3 · vl2ggplot — Vega-Lite translation showcase</footer>
<script src="assets/site.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
